.direnv/**

# Build output and installed dependencies, ignored repo-wide as well as by each
# package's own .gitignore. The per-package files are not enough on their own:
# they are tracked content, so deleting a package directory takes its .gitignore
# with it, and whatever `node_modules/` and `dist/` are left on disk become
# visible at that exact moment. That has happened twice here — 9028 files
# snapshotted during the 0.1.0 reset, 113MB during the rookery extraction.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.direnv/

# Beads is machine-local in this repo, as it is everywhere else. Nothing under
# `.beads/` is tracked — not the db, not its locks, and not `issues.jsonl`.
# Tracking the export was tried here (see the CLAUDE.md note) and reverted: br
# reimports from that file, so a copy pulled from another machine can silently
# revert a close, and every mutation on two machines is a whole-file conflict in
# a file no one reads by hand.
.beads/**
.abacus/**
